<title>FRANCE: Lafarge nine-month sales up 4.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Lafarge nine-month sales up 4.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover			  26,087   vs   24,961</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>	   Cement		     12,029   vs   11,122</p>
<p>	   Concrete and aggregate  7,250   vs    6,847</p>
<p>	   Plaster		     2,451   vs    2,398</p>
<p>	   Special materials	 4,358   vs    4,283</p>
<p>	   Other			     0   vs	310</p>
<p>NOTE - Lafarge gave its sales figures in a statement. It said the turnover rise was a result of the group's recent development and of an &quot;encouraging&quot; quarterly trend. Third quarter sales rose in central Europe and Canada, the United States and emerging markets, but the French building industry remained depressed.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom 33+1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
